{"findings":[{"file":"spacy/pipeline/pipes.pyx","line":97,"what_goes_wrong":"The base streaming pipeline calls `len(tuple)` instead of `len(predictions)`, so any subclass that returns the documented `(scores, tensors)` pair crashes.","trigger":"Call inherited `Pipe.pipe()` on a subclass whose `predict(docs)` returns a two-item tuple; `ClozeMultitask.predict` does this.","expected":"The pair should be unpacked and passed to `set_annotations`, as `Pipe.__call__` already does.","actual":"`TypeError: object of type 'type' has no len()` is raised before annotations are set.","confidence":"high","verified_by_running":true,"reproduction":"from pathlib import Path\n\nsource = Path(\"spacy/pipeline/pipes.pyx\").read_text(encoding=\"utf8\")\nstart = source.index(\"class Pipe(object):\")\nend = source.index(\"    def predict(self, docs):\", start)\nUtil = type(\"Util\", (), {\"minibatch\": staticmethod(lambda stream, size: [list(stream)])})\nnamespace = {\"util\": Util}\nexec(source[start:end], namespace)\nPipe = namespace[\"Pipe\"]\nDummy = type(\"Dummy\", (Pipe,), {\n    \"__init__\": lambda self, vocab: setattr(self, \"model\", object()),\n    \"predict\": lambda self, docs: ([0], [0]),\n    \"set_annotations\": lambda self, docs, scores, tensors=None: None,\n})\nassert list(Dummy(None).pipe([object()]))"},{"file":"spacy/util.py","line":552,"what_goes_wrong":"`minibatch_by_words` consumes an extra item after a batch exactly reaches its requested word count.","trigger":"Call `minibatch_by_words([['a'], ['b'], ['c']], 2, tuples=False)`, where each item has two words under the default `len` counter.","expected":"The first batch should contain `[['a'], ['b']]` (two words) and the second `[['c']]`.","actual":"The first batch contains all three items (six words), because the loop continues when the remaining count is zero.","confidence":"high","verified_by_running":true,"reproduction":"from pathlib import Path\nimport itertools\n\nsource = Path(\"spacy/util.py\").read_text(encoding=\"utf8\")\nstart = source.index(\"def minibatch_by_words\")\nend = source.index(\"\\ndef itershuffle\", start)\nnamespace = {\"itertools\": itertools}\nexec(source[start:end], namespace)\n\nbatches = list(namespace[\"minibatch_by_words\"]([['a'], ['b'], ['c']], 2, tuples=False))\nassert batches == [[['a'], ['b']], [['c']]]"}],"what_examined":"I inspected core Python/Cython pipeline, serialization, conversion, scoring, lookup, lemmatization, and utility code; used Ruff only as a lead; and executed focused isolated reproducers from the checked-in source. The supplied interpreter lacks spaCy runtime dependencies (for example, `thinc`), so the project test suite could not import."}
